course: dictionary
lesson: 6643
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one you need. Nuclear comes from nucleus, the tiny centre of an atom. Atoms are far too small to see, yet they hold a huge amount of energy.
explain: «Big nuclear submarines make their own oxygen from seawater using electricity.» Here nuclear describes the submarines, so it means powered by energy from atoms. The sentence is about power, not about families or bombs.
explain: Now read «a nuclear family». The same word means something different here: a mother, father and their children living together. When a word surprises you, read the whole sentence and ask which meaning fits.
fact: Nuclear means to do with the nucleus, the tiny centre of an atom.
fact: «Nuclear power» means power made using the energy stored in atoms.
fact: «Nuclear family» means a mother, father and their children living together.
fact: «Go nuclear» is slang for getting extremely angry or doing something extreme.
fact: Nuclear power and nuclear weapons are serious topics, so people discuss how to keep them safe.
exercise: «Big nuclear submarines make their own oxygen from seawater using electricity.» In this sentence, what does nuclear mean? | *Powered by energy from atoms | Made of wood | A mother, father and their children | Very angry
exercise: Ella says a «nuclear family» is about bombs. What is a nuclear family? | A family that lives in a big city | *A mother, father and their children living together | A family that is very angry | A group of atoms stuck together
exercise: Which word means the tiny centre of an atom? | *nucleus | submarine | oxygen | energy
test: «He went nuclear when he saw the broken window.» What does go nuclear mean here? | Fell fast asleep | Started a new job | *Got extremely angry | Ran very quickly
test: The Dragonfly is «a nuclear-powered drone helicopter». What does nuclear-powered tell you? | It runs on sunlight alone | *It runs on energy from atoms | It runs on wind | It runs on batteries only
exam: Which phrase means a mother, father and their children living together? | nuclear power | nuclear bomb | go nuclear | *nuclear family
